      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 239.91,
      "end_seconds": 248.13,
      "duration_seconds": 8.22,
      "text": "it's reasonable to be concerned, but right now an infected diabetic foot ulcer is my leading thought, not anything worse"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 263.84,
      "end_seconds": 293.11,
      "duration_seconds": 29.27,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an X-ray of the foot for possible osteomyelitis. Let's book blood tests to look into infected ulcer. I'd like to arrange a wound swab for infected ulcer. You'll be taking co-amoxiclav 625 milligrams three times a day seven days. That should help with infected ulcer. Keep the weight off the foot and keep the dressing dry. I'm going to send a referral to the diabetic foot clinic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 293.78,
      "end_seconds": 303.73,
      "duration_seconds": 9.95,
      "text": "do get help quickly if the symptoms get worse we'll catch up in two days have I covered everything you wanted?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
